  "summary_en": "El Salvador's Robotic Technologies Law (Decree 340, July 2025) sets a framework and incentives for robotics. It gives the National AI Agency (ANIA) a robotics division with risk classification (three tiers), safety standards, import authorisation and role-based responsibilities, recognises ISO robot safety standards, and promotes innovation, education and testing.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "ANIA creates a Robotics Division to enforce the law, classify risk and issue technical safety norms",
   "Three-tier risk classification (basic, intermediate, high) of design, development and manufacturing operations",
   "Role-based responsibilities for manufacturers, integrators, deployers, operators and end users",
   "Official catalogue recognises ISO/TS 15066, ISO 10218, ISO 13482 and IEC 61508; import authorisation by ANIA via Customs",
   "Fiscal incentives, pilot testing, controlled test environments and robotics education; drones and hobbyists largely excluded"
  ],
